title: Vikram_Day1
tags: 
position: -7,-175
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite TeaStall>>

// Scene Setup - Day 1 at the tea stall during evening rush
After noticing the long queue outside Vikram's tea stall and hearing his mother mention how hard small vendors work, Raju visits during the busy evening period to see if the hardworking tea seller might need assistance.

Aromatic clouds of cardamom and ginger fill the air around Vikram's modest tea stall. The skilled vendor prepares fresh chai for a steady stream of customers. Vikram moves between boiling milk, measuring spices, and serving steaming cups, but the sweat on his brow suggests even his experience is being tested by today's heavy demand.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Tired">>
Vikram: Beta, terrible timing and perfect timing all at once!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Worried">>
Vikram: Everyone wants fresh tea at the same moment, and I'm just one person trying to brew, serve, and manage money all simultaneously.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Anxious">>
Vikram: Look at this queue - it's going to take forever to serve everyone properly.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Vikram uncle, you look completely overwhelmed! Is there anything I can do to help?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: I have some free time and I'd love to learn about tea preparation and small business operations.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Skeptical">>
Vikram: Help? Beta, running a tea stall isn't child's play.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Serious">>
Vikram: Every cup must taste perfect, customers expect fast service, and one mistake with ingredients or money can ruin my reputation.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Worried">>
Vikram: This business feeds my family - it can't afford errors.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: I understand it's serious work, uncle. But I'm careful and I learn quickly.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Maybe I could start with something simple, just to help reduce your stress during busy periods?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Irritated">>
Vikram: Simple? Child, there's nothing simple about creating perfect tea!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Serious">>
Vikram: Every blend requires precise spice ratios, milk must be heated to exact temperature.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Worried">>
Vikram: And customers have specific preferences developed over years. One bad cup and they never return.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: That's exactly why I want to help, uncle!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: You've built such loyal customers who depend on your quality tea. Surely there's some small way I could assist without affecting your standards?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Quizzical">>
Vikram: You really want to learn about tea preparation?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Skeptical">>
Vikram: Even knowing how demanding customers can be when their chai isn't perfect, how precise ingredient measurement must be, how exhausting these long days become?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: I'm not afraid of demanding work or critical customers, uncle.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: My father always says that small businesses are the heart of any community, and I want to understand what that really means.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
As Raju exits the bustling tea stall, he carries deep appreciation for the complexity of tea-making operations and strengthened determination to prove his offer represents genuine commitment. The intricate balance Vikram demonstrates has revealed sophisticated expertise successful tea vendors require.

<<set $Vikram_Day = 2>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===

title: Vikram_Day2
tags: 
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite TeaStall>>

// Scene Setup - Day 2 during morning preparation
Despite yesterday's introduction to the demanding world of tea vending, Raju returns during morning preparation, hoping to observe how Vikram organizes his ingredients and prepares for the day's service.

The tea stall emanates methodical preparation in the early morning. Vikram systematically arranges spices, checks milk quality, and organizes his workspace with precision. The peaceful atmosphere contrasts sharply with yesterday's rush, revealing careful planning that enables consistent quality.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Smiling">>
Vikram: Back again, beta? I thought yesterday's reality check about the complexity of tea preparation might have discouraged you.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Skeptical">>
Vikram: Most young people lose interest when they discover that real quality takes years to develop.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Actually, uncle, watching you work yesterday made me more fascinated, not less.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: I've never seen anyone use such simple ingredients to create beverages that bring people so much satisfaction and comfort.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Disappointed">>
Vikram: Fascinated? Beta, society doesn't value tea vendors the way they should.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Sad">>
Vikram: People need our service daily but don't respect the skill involved. They want cheap, fast chai instead of quality preparation that takes time and expertise.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: How did you learn such precise tea-making techniques?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Curious">>
Raju: Did someone teach you, or did you develop these recipes through experience?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Proud">>
Vikram: My father ran a tea stall before me, and I started learning the family recipes at age twelve.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Serious">>
Vikram: Twenty-five years I've been perfecting these blends, learning customer preferences, and building relationships.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Disappointed">>
Vikram: But young people today want modern jobs - they think food service is beneath them.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: That must be disappointing, uncle.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: Seeing such valuable knowledge and customer relationships being undervalued by people who don't understand the skill required.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Proud">>
Vikram: They don't understand that every cup of tea represents hospitality, comfort, and community connection.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Serious">>
Vikram: When people start their day with my chai, I'm contributing to their energy and mood.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Smiling">>
Vikram: When they gather here to chat, I'm providing social space that brings neighbors together.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: That's exactly why I want to learn, uncle!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Tea preparation creates immediate comfort and social connection for people's daily lives. I don't want to miss the chance to understand such meaningful work.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Quizzical">>
Vikram: You keep expressing interest in learning, but tea service means different levels of responsibility and skill.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vikram" "Serious">>
Vikram: What exactly do you think you could contribute to established tea preparation?

<<HideAllCharacters>>
As their conversation concludes with Vikram's direct question, Raju recognizes his persistent interest has moved beyond polite dismissal into serious consideration. The revelation of the vendor's disappointment about society's undervaluation has transformed his motivation from curiosity into genuine respect.

